<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann IX von Haugwitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1524">1524</a>–<a href="/years/1595">1595</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann IX von Haugwitz was the last Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a>, elected in 1555. Under pressure from Elector Augustus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> he ceded the bishopric's lands to the electorate and resigned in 1581, then became a Lutheran and married. His resignation ended the bishops' secular rule.</p></div>
